1
00:00:00,272 --> 00:00:03,380
Now, as you can tell, if you take a look at

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:06,488
the official HTMX reference page,

3
00:00:07,386 --> 00:00:09,757
HTMX offers quite a few

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:13,122
attributes you can add and some other

5
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:15,813
features which we'll also explore throughout

6
00:00:15,813 --> 00:00:16,278
this course.

7
00:00:17,239 --> 00:00:19,707
And whilst I won't cover all those

8
00:00:19,819 --> 00:00:22,110
attributes in this section here already,

9
00:00:22,478 --> 00:00:25,186
since this is just the essentials section,

10
00:00:25,587 --> 00:00:28,743
there is one other really essential

11
00:00:29,416 --> 00:00:31,899
attribute that I do wanna cover here, and

12
00:00:31,915 --> 00:00:35,040
that's the hx-trigger attribute.

13
00:00:35,985 --> 00:00:40,776
And the hx-trigger attribute can be added to

14
00:00:40,872 --> 00:00:41,417
an element

15
00:00:41,993 --> 00:00:45,919
to control how exactly the request will be

16
00:00:45,919 --> 00:00:46,255
triggered.

17
00:00:47,072 --> 00:00:48,947
So hx-get defines

18
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,870
which kind of request,

19
00:00:51,463 --> 00:00:54,427
a GET request to this path should be sent,

20
00:00:54,988 --> 00:00:57,519
and hx-trigger then configures

21
00:00:58,096 --> 00:01:01,065
when that request should be sent, so how it

22
00:01:01,065 --> 00:01:01,900
should be triggered.

23
00:01:02,847 --> 00:01:03,296
And of course,

24
00:01:03,970 --> 00:01:06,153
it worked without that attribute as well,

25
00:01:06,442 --> 00:01:09,587
right? A request was sent when we clicked

26
00:01:09,587 --> 00:01:12,331
the button. And the reason for that is that

27
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:13,487
by default,

28
00:01:14,145 --> 00:01:18,189
requests will be sent when the most obvious

29
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:20,901
event, you could say, the event that makes

30
00:01:20,901 --> 00:01:24,079
the most sense for a given element occurs.

31
00:01:24,741 --> 00:01:26,325
For example, for a form,

32
00:01:27,004 --> 00:01:29,655
that would be the submit event. For a

33
00:01:29,688 --> 00:01:33,503
button, and actually for most elements, it's

34
00:01:33,746 --> 00:01:34,535
a click event.

35
00:01:36,049 --> 00:01:38,223
And therefore, if you wanna send that

36
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:39,784
request upon a click

37
00:01:40,396 --> 00:01:42,667
on the element on which the attribute is

38
00:01:42,812 --> 00:01:43,037
added,

39
00:01:43,635 --> 00:01:45,888
you don't need hx-trigger.

40
00:01:47,414 --> 00:01:49,509
But you do need it if you wanna send the

41
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:52,458
request when some other event occurs.

42
00:01:53,172 --> 00:01:56,104
And you can configure quite a lot of things

43
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,555
here. You can, for example, also make sure

44
00:01:59,020 --> 00:01:59,597
that it's

45
00:02:00,126 --> 00:02:03,074
a click event with the Control key pressed.

46
00:02:03,506 --> 00:02:05,445
That could be done as well. And you see the

47
00:02:05,445 --> 00:02:08,233
syntax for that here in the docs, though you

48
00:02:08,233 --> 00:02:10,203
of course don't need to go through them

49
00:02:10,235 --> 00:02:13,247
here. I'll show you some important examples

50
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,609
here throughout this course.

51
00:02:15,442 --> 00:02:18,807
So let's therefore say that here for demo

52
00:02:19,031 --> 00:02:19,576
purposes,

53
00:02:20,233 --> 00:02:22,914
I wanna send the request if I

54
00:02:23,769 --> 00:02:24,286
enter

55
00:02:25,399 --> 00:02:28,110
this element with my mouse, so if I hover

56
00:02:28,691 --> 00:02:29,191
over it,

57
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,813
if I also at the same time have the Control

58
00:02:32,912 --> 00:02:33,588
key pressed.

59
00:02:35,737 --> 00:02:37,025
If I save that all

60
00:02:38,071 --> 00:02:40,663
and I reload here, you'll notice that if I

61
00:02:40,663 --> 00:02:40,840
now

62
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:44,415
mouse over Learn More, nothing happens.

63
00:02:45,171 --> 00:02:45,932
If I click it,

64
00:02:46,578 --> 00:02:47,440
nothing happens.

65
00:02:48,263 --> 00:02:50,877
But if I now hold the Control key, which I'm

66
00:02:50,909 --> 00:02:51,438
now doing,

67
00:02:52,272 --> 00:02:55,127
and I hover over it, now the request was

68
00:02:55,255 --> 00:02:57,452
sent and this is loaded.

69
00:02:58,687 --> 00:03:02,455
Now you can also define multiple events that

70
00:03:02,455 --> 00:03:05,663
should trigger this request simply by

71
00:03:05,663 --> 00:03:08,437
separating them with a comma here in that

72
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:10,297
value for hx-trigger.

73
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:13,168
So for example, here we could also add

74
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:13,617
click.

75
00:03:15,124 --> 00:03:17,128
And now this would make sure that this

76
00:03:17,128 --> 00:03:20,800
request here is sent whenever we mouse over

77
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:23,430
the button, if the Control key is pressed,

78
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:27,150
or if we just click the button without the

79
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:29,523
requirement of the Control key being

80
00:03:29,635 --> 00:03:30,036
pressed.

81
00:03:31,383 --> 00:03:34,253
And with that, if I save that, if I reload

82
00:03:34,365 --> 00:03:34,974
this page,

83
00:03:35,792 --> 00:03:37,492
you'll notice that if I hover over it,

84
00:03:37,636 --> 00:03:38,422
nothing happens.

85
00:03:39,256 --> 00:03:41,340
If I hover over it with the Control key

86
00:03:41,404 --> 00:03:42,993
pressed, this is loaded,

87
00:03:43,587 --> 00:03:45,755
and if I click it, this is also loaded.

88
00:03:46,718 --> 00:03:50,299
And that's how you can use hx-trigger to

89
00:03:50,331 --> 00:03:51,728
configure in detail

90
00:03:52,338 --> 00:03:52,531
when

91
00:03:53,141 --> 00:03:56,738
exactly that request is sent. You don't need

92
00:03:56,738 --> 00:03:58,648
it if you're happy with the default, which

93
00:03:58,937 --> 00:04:00,623
in most cases is a click,

94
00:04:01,233 --> 00:04:03,706
but if you have some other specific event

95
00:04:03,803 --> 00:04:05,392
for which the request should be sent,

96
00:04:05,970 --> 00:04:07,560
hx-trigger is your friend.
